          %h4#wilson
            Scott Wilson,
            = succeed "." do
              %em Some algebra relat4ed to mapping spaces and applications
          %p
            Wilson defined a
            %em partial algebra
            as a lax
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            from the category of finite sets to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(j \coprod k) \rightarrow A(j) \otimes A(k)
            is a quasi-isomorphism. He showed how these pop up in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            all the time.
          %p
            (Remark: this formula is the basis for
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} commutative algebra in an (infinity,1)-category
            in general and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-category
            in particular).
          %p
            For instance, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is any space and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a partial algebra, the resulting total complex can be seen as a generalization of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Bartlett"} Bruce
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is the interval, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the partial algebra of forms on a Riemannian manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
