                %a{:href => "http://www.math.sunysb.edu/~blafard/tex/sum09/ow_june_11.pdf"} Notes by Gabriel Drummond-Cole
            %li
              %p
                Urs’s personal nLab write-up on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Background+fields+in+twisted+differential+nonabelian+cohomology"} Background fields in twisted differential nonabelian cohomology
                (and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/files/OWR_2009_28.pdf"} pdf
          %h4#henriques
            André Henriques,
            = succeed "." do
              %em Invertible conformal nets
          %p
            In this talk, Henriques described joint work with Chris Douglas and Arthur Bartels on the program of establishing an equivalence between full conformal field theories and ‘conformal nets’. Preliminary write-ups of this work is available on his
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uu.nl/people/henrique/"} webpage
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebra"} factorization algebra
            (in the sense of Costello’s talk) on 1-dimensional manifolds taking values in the bicategory of Von Neumann algebras with
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            %em
              index
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(A)
              of a conformal net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is defined to be the statistical dimension of the vacuum sector
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              assigns to arcs on the unit circle. He stated the following result.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+net"} conformal net
              is invertible if and only if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(A)=1
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(A) \lt \infty
          %h5#resources_12 Resources
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.sunysb.edu/~blafard/tex/sum09/ow_june_11.pdf"} Notes by Gabriel Drummond-Cole
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+Workshop%2C+June+2009+--+Thursday%2C+June+11"} Notes by Urs Schreiber
            %li
